hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"336","Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi told us, Abu Dawud told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Abu Qalaba told him, that Abu Al-Malih Al-Hudhali told him, he said: We were with Buraydah Al-Aslami on a campaign on a cloudy day, and he said: Arrive early to pray, for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever abandons the afternoon prayer, his work will be nullified.” Al-Hussein bin Harith Abu Ammar narrated to us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, the companion of Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qalabah: With this Like him, except that he said: “His work has been vain.”"
